==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈhɪd.iː.ʌs/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈhɪd.i.əs/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-hideous.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Extremely or shockingly [[ugly]].
#* {{RQ:Macaulay History of England|passage=the Duke's army departed unmolested : but the highway along which he retired presented a piteous and '''hideous''' spectacle.}}
# Having a very [[unpleasant]] or frightening sound
#* {{RQ:Defoe Robinson Crusoe|passage=He started up, growling at first, but finding his leg broken, fell down again; and then got upon three legs, and gave the most '''hideous''' roar that ever I heard.}}
# Hateful; shocking.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Twelfth Night|1|5|passage=Sure, you have some '''hideous''' matter to deliver.}}
# Morally offensive; shocking; detestable.
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1851
|author={{w|Herman Melville}}
|title={{w|Moby Dick}}
|section=Chapter 9
|passage=when the wind is shrieking, and the men are yelling, and every plank thunders with trampling feet right over Jonah’s head; in all this raging tumult, Jonah sleeps his '''hideous''' sleep.}}

